    "html": "<p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Worth 10% of your final course grade. Maximum score: 10 points.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Purpose</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Complete three dated field notes from Weeks 2 and 3. Start each note with a specific example from class, public example, or low-risk digital-system encounter. Use a course concept to explain the system rather than only describe it.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Each note must include</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">• The date and specific system or example.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">• What the system did: sorted, ranked, watched, recommended, denied, or enabled.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">• One course concept, explained in your own words.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">• One piece of course or public evidence.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">• Who benefits, who carries the cost, and what remains uncertain.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Format and boundary</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Aim for 150 to 200 words or a one-to-two-minute audio note per entry. Do not identify classmates or disclose private information. The dated example and your changing explanation are required process evidence. Generative AI may not create or rewrite entries.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">How Set 1 is graded</p><p><br></p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Specific dated evidence: 2.5 points.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">course concept use: 3 points.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">analysis of power and effect: 3 points.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">reflection and communication: 1.5 points.</li></ul><p><br></p><h3>How to post your journal entries</h3><p><br></p><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:28px;\"><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Open this journal in Blackboard and find Entries. Start a separate entry for each required date or example.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Write directly in the journal editor. Put the entry number and date at the top. You do not need to upload a Word document.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">If you choose an audio entry, attach the recording and a transcript, or add a Seneca-accessible recording link.</li><li style=\"margin:0 0 8px;line-height:1.6;\">Select Post, then reopen the entry to confirm it is there. You may edit your entries through the submission window stated below. Only you and the teaching team can read this journal.</li></ul><p><br></p><h3>Your work and permitted tools</h3><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0;line-height:1.6;\">Use your own observations, choices, explanations, and sources. Do not use generative AI to write or rewrite your submission, invent experiences or evidence, or create narration in your place. You may use spelling, dictation, screen-reader, captioning, and accessibility tools that do not generate the course content. Ask me before using a tool if you are unsure.</p><p><br></p><h3>Deadlines and submission window</h3><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">Released: September 15, 2026 at 12:01 a.m. Eastern.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\"><strong>Due: September 25, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern.</strong></p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">The 48-hour no-penalty submission window ends September 27, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. Eastern. Routine extension requests must arrive before the posted due date, not during this window.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\">If Blackboard labels work submitted within the allowed window as late, that label does not mean a penalty applies. Work after the applicable window receives zero unless an extension or exception is approved. Unexpected emergencies and approved accommodations are considered separately.</p><p><br></p><p style=\"margin:0 0 16px;line-height:1.6;\"><a href=\"deadline-policy.html\">Read the full Deadlines and Extensions policy</a>.</p>",
